<title>ZIMBABWE: PRESS DIGEST - ZIMBABWE - AUG 4.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - ZIMBABWE - AUG 4.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the leading stories in Zimbabwe's state-owned Herald newspaper on Monday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>THE HERALD</p>
<p>- Seven Zimbabwean textile companies have been liquidated since January resulting in the loss of hundreds of jobs.</p>
<p>- The United States Agency for Development has reduced its budget for projects in Africa to U.S.$820,000 from U.S.$4 million, United States Information Service director in Zimbabwe William Lukasavich said at the weekend.</p>
<p>-- Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
